  "details": "When a friend request comes in, it's hard to decide where it comes from and why he/she choose me.\n\nSo i need more information to accept it or cancel it.\n\nI need information about:\n- friend level (visitor / new user / trusted etc...)\nThis is important and it's easy to show it.\n- friend linked to other friend (due friends+ setting, they come and i don't know which friend is linked with her/him) \nIt should show some links to one of my friends. If one of my friend is showed in the window, then i can accept it. If there is no link, i can cancel it.\n\nOptional add reason why he/she want friend me is also welcome. \nFrom now, click on image and only 3 buttons to decide? Why so less information? There is plenty room in the window for more information about the user.\n\nBecause you can click on existing friends, you will see small information and status. So why not with requests?",
